  "アース(接地)": "Earth",
  "アース(接地)機械の外箱を地面につなぐ線です。漏電しても、電気は抵抗の小さいアースへ流れ、外箱の電圧が低くおさえられます。アースがないと、外箱が100V近くになり、触った人の体を通って電気が地面へ流れます。": "The earthing line is a line connecting the outer box of an earthing machine to the ground. Even if there is a leakage, the electricity flows to the earth with small resistance, and the voltage of the outer box can be kept low. Without earth, the outer box will become near 100V, and electricity will flow through the body of the person who touches it to the ground.",
  "アースがあると漏れ電流が分かれ、外箱の電圧と人に流れる電流が下がる": "The leakage current is divided by the earth, and the voltage of the outer box and the current flowing to the person are reduced.",
