  "メガーは測るときに試験電圧を出します。電気が来ている回路に当てると、メガー自身や、回路につながった機械の電子部品を壊すおそれがあり、感電の危険もあります。メガーは必ずブレーカーを切って、電気が来ていないことを確かめてから使います。": "Meggers produce a test voltage when they measure. If applied to a circuit with electricity, there is a risk of damaging the megger itself or the electronic components of the machine connected to the circuit, and there is also a risk of electric shock. Megger always turns off the breaker and makes sure that there is no electricity coming in before using it.",
