  "図の線を選ぶと、つなぐ端子を確認できます。": "Selecting a line in the diagram shows the terminals to be connected.",
  "図は": "The figures are .",
  "図はDC24V用LED表示灯の一例です。内部の抵抗をLEDと直列につなぎ、流れる電流を抑えます。LEDが光ると、手前のレンズを通して見えます。": "The figure shows an example of LED indicator light for DC24V. The internal resistor is connected in series with the LED and the flowing current is suppressed. When the LED lights up, you can see through the lens in front of you.",
  "図は切替接点1組の例です。コイルに通電すると鉄心が": "The figure shows an example of one set of switching contacts. When you put an electric current into the coil, the core is formed.",
  "図は切替接点1組の例です。コイルに通電すると鉄心が接極子を引き寄せ、絶縁部分を介して可動接点を押します。共通端子（COM）の接続先がb側からa側に切り替わり、通電をやめると戻しばねでb側に戻ります。": "The figure shows an example of one set of switching contacts. When the coil is powered, the core pulls the contact poles and pushes the movable contact through the insulating part. The connection point of the common terminal (COM) switches from the b-side to the a-side, and when the power is stopped, it returns to the b-sides by the reverse pin.",
  "図は横取付の磁石式です。水面が上がると浮きが持ち上がり、アームの反対側の": "The figure shows the magnetic formula of the laterally mounted magnet. When the water level rises, the float lifts up and the other side of the arm is lifted.",
  "図は横取付の磁石式です。水面が上がると浮きが持ち上がり、アームの反対側の磁石が下がります。磁石の動きが隔壁の向こうのスイッチに伝わり、接点が切り替わります。": "The figure shows the magnetic formula of the laterally mounted magnet. When the water level rises, the float rises and the magnet on the opposite side of the arm descends. The movement of the magnet is transmitted to the switch on the other side of the wall, and the contacts are switched.",
  "図は発振回路を内蔵した電磁式です。直流電源を入れると、内部の回路がコイルの電流を周期的に変えます。磁石とコイルが振動板を引く力が強弱を繰り返し、板が震えて音が出ます。": "The figure shows an electromagnetic formula incorporating an oscillating circuit. When a DC power supply is inserted, the internal circuit periodically changes the current of the coil. The magnet and coil pull the vibrating plate with a repeatedly changing force, and the plate shakes and makes a sound.",
  "図は誘導モーターの断面です。外側の固定子のコイルが": "The figure shows a cross section of the induction motor. The coil of the external fixer.",
  "図は誘導モーターの断面です。外側の固定子のコイルが回転磁界をつくると、内側の回転子の導体に電流が誘導され、回す力が生じます。負荷を動かすとき、回転子は矢印が示す磁界と同じ向きに、少し遅れて回ります。": "The figure shows a cross section of the induction motor. When the coil of the outer fixer creates a rotating magnetic field, a current is induced in the conductor of the inner rotor, and a rotating force is generated. When the load is moved, the rotor rotates in the same direction as the magnetic field shown by the arrow, with a slight delay.",
