  "測温抵抗体 Pt100": "Pt100 thermometer resistor",
  "測温抵抗体 Pt100白金の線は、温度が上がると電気抵抗が増えます。0℃で100Ω、1℃につき約0.385Ω増えます。温調器はこの抵抗を測って温度に直しています。": "Pt100 resistance temperature detector. Platinum's resistance rises with temperature. It is 100 Ω at 0 °C and rises by about 0.385 Ω per 1 °C. The controller measures resistance to determine temperature.",
  "湿気": "Humidity",
  "湿気で絶縁が少し悪くなりました。通電すると、外箱に電気がもれやすくなります。": "The insulation has become a little worse because of the humidity. When the electrical current is passed, the outer box becomes more electrically attractive.",
  "満水": "Mansu",
  "満水のスイッチが効かないと、タンクから水があふれる": "If the full water switch doesn't work, the tank will overflow.",
  "準備中": "Preparing",
  "溶けて切れ": "Melt.",
  "漏れ電流": "Leakage current",
  "漏れ電流(全体)": "Leakage current (total)",
  "漏れ電流と、人に流れる電流(mA)。目盛りは10倍ずつ": "The leakage current and the current flowing to the person (mA) are measured. We're going to have ten times the scale.",
  "漏電": "Electrical leakage",
  "漏電で切れた": "It's a power leak.",
  "漏電で行きと帰りに差ができ、設定した感度に達するとこのブレーカーが切れる": "The leakage can cause a difference in the return and return, and when the set sensitivity is reached, this breaker will be switched off.",
  "漏電と絶縁の部屋": "The leakage and insulated room.",
  "漏電と絶縁の部屋です。洗濯機は分電盤の漏電ブレーカーから電気をもらい、外箱はアース線で地面につながっています。画面の「洗濯機の中」で水がかかったを選び、ブレーカーの動きを見よう。": "It's a leakage and insulated room. The washing machine receives electricity from the leakage breaker in the distribution panel, and the outer box is connected to the ground with an earth wire. Choose \"Water in the washing machine\" on the screen and see the breaker's movement.",
  "漏電ブレーカー": "Leakage circuit breaker",
  "漏電ブレーカー:行きと帰りの電流の差(漏れ)を見て切れます。": "Leakage breaker: It can cut off the difference (leakage) of the going and returning current.",
  "漏電ブレーカーが切れました": "The leak breaker is off.",
  "漏電ブレーカーが切れました。行き(L)と帰り(N)の電流に": "The leakage breaker is off. The outgoing current (L) and the returning current (N)",
  "漏電ブレーカーが切れる値": "Leakage breaker",
  "漏電ブレーカーの感度より小さい電流だったので切れませんでした。": "The current was smaller than the sensitivity of the leakage breaker, so it could not be cut off.",
  "漏電ブレーカー中のZCT(零相変流器)という輪に、行きの線(L)と帰りの線(N)を両方通しています。ふだんは行きと帰りの電流が同じで打ち消し合いますが、漏電すると差が出て、この教材の高速形は差が設定値（15・30mA）に達すると0.05秒で切れる設定です。": "The leakage circuit breaker is a circuit with a zero phase transformer (ZCT) in which both the incoming and returning lines are connected. The high speed version of this teaching material is set to be cut off in 0.05 seconds when the difference reaches the set value (15, 30mA).",
  "漏電・メガー": "Leakage Megger",
  "灰色:トランジスタの入り切り": "Gray: Transistor cut-out",
  "点滅": "Flash",
  "点灯": "Lights on.",
  "点線は定格電流（約9A）": "The point line is rated current (about 9A).",
  "無通電：COMとb側が導通": "No power: COM and b side are connected.",
  "照明": "Lighting",
  "照明スイッチ": "Lighting switch",
  "熱で曲がる": "It's bending in heat.",
  "熱は": "Fever.",
  "熱動電磁式": "Thermodynamic electromagnetic equation",
  "熱電対 K": "Thermocouple K",
  "熱電対 K2種類の金属をつなぐと、先端と根元の温度差で小さな電圧が生まれます(K型で1℃あたり約0.041mV)。とても小さい電圧なので、+と−をまちがえると逆の値になります。": "When two types of metals K are connected to a thermocouple, a small voltage is generated by the temperature difference between the tip and the root (approximately 0.041mV per 1℃ in the K type). Because the voltage is very small, if you turn + and -, the values will be the opposite.",
  "熱電対K": "Thermocouple K",
  "熱電対の+−を逆に": "The thermocouple's +- is reversed.",
  "熱電対の+と−を逆につなぐと、温度が上がっているのに下がって見える": "The thermocouple is reversed, so that the temperature appears to be higher but lower.",
  "熱電対を選んでいるときだけ影響します。センサーを「熱電対 K」にしてみよう。": "The effect is only when the thermocouple is selected. The sensor is a thermocouple K.",
