  "発見と故障ノート": "Discovery and fault notes",
  "発見はこのブラウザーに自動保存されます。": "Discoveries will be saved automatically in this browser.",
  "発見ノート": "Discovering Notes",
  "白い樹脂": "White resin",
  "白金の線は、温度が上がると": "The platinum line, when it gets hot,",
  "盤の+24Vを電源側に、リレーやランプに向かう線を負荷側につなぎます。遮断の原因を取り除いて手動で復帰すると、回路を再び使えます。": "Connect the +24V of the plate to the power side and the wire to the relay or lamp to the load side. If you remove the cause of the interruption and manually reconnect, the circuit can be used again.",
  "盤のV・Vはコイルに電気を入れる2端子です。この弁は通電すると開く常時閉（NC）形です。": "The V and V of the plate are two terminals that feed electricity into the coil. The valve is a constantly closed (NC) type which opens when power is applied.",
  "盤の下にある緑の": "The green under the plate.",
  "盤の下にある緑の起動を押して、ランプが点いたら離してみよう。キー 1 でも試せます。押している間はリレー R1 の接点が閉じています。": "Press the green start button under the plate and try to unplug it when the lamp lights up. You can also try key 1. The contact of relay R1 is closed while the button is pressed.",
  "盤の図ではファンなどの入力を1・2、正逆転装置の指令入力をF（正転）・R（逆転）・C（共通）で表しています。": "In the diagram of the plate, the inputs of the fan, etc. are represented by 1 and 2, and the command input of the reversing device is represented by F (reverse), R (reverse) and C (common).",
  "盤の外から来た電線と盤内の配線をつないだり、電源を複数の回路に分けたりする部品です。": "It is a part that connects wires coming from outside the plate with wiring inside the plate, or that divides the power supply into multiple circuits.",
  "盤の左上のブレーカーをONにして、赤の停止灯だけが点くか確認しよう。": "Turn the top left switch of the plate ON and check that only the red stop light is lit.",
  "盤の接続：": "Disc connection:",
  "盤の端子を2つ、順にクリックする。": "Click two terminals of the plate in succession.",
  "盤の線と同じ番号の線が光ります": "The same number of lines will light up as the ones on the disc .",
  "盤の部品をクリックすると、その部品の中身が見られます": "Click on a piece of the disc to see what's inside it",
  "盤の配線をすべて外す": "Remove all wiring from the plate.",
  "盤を拡大して配線する（左右にスクロール）": "Enlarge the plate and wiring (scroll left and right)",
  "目標(SV)": "Target (SV)",
  "目標は": "What is the goal?",
  "目標は60℃。まず「時間の速さ」を10倍にして、ON/OFF制御の水温が目標の上下を行き来する様子を見よう。次にPIDに切り替えて、グラフを比べてみよう。": "The target temperature was 60℃. First, we increase the speed of time by 10 times and see how the water temperature of the ON/OFF control moves up and down the target. Now let's switch to PID and compare the graphs.",
  "目標を上げる": "Raise the target.",
  "目標を下げる": "I'm lowering the target.",
  "直したあとの正しい動作": "The correct action after correction",
  "直入れ": "Direct into the game.",
  "直入れ:電源をそのままモーターにつなぐ一番簡単な始動方法。電磁接触器(MC)1つで入り切りします。": "Direct plug: The simplest starting method by connecting the power supply to the motor as it is. The contact is cut with one electromagnetic contactor (MC).",
  "直入れ始動": "Direct start",
  "直入れ始動は、定格の約6倍の大電流が一瞬流れる": "The direct start is a momentary flow of a large current about 6 times the rated current.",
  "直入れ始動誘導モーターを止まった状態で電源につなぐと、回転する磁界と回転子の速度差（すべり）が最大になり、大きな始動電流が流れます。この教材では定格の約6倍です。回転が上がるにつれて電流は下がります。": "When the direct‐start inductive motor is connected to the power supply in the stopped state, the difference in speed (slip) between the rotating magnetic field and the rotor is maximized, and a large starting current flows. The grades are about 6 times higher than the standard grades in this textbook. The current decreases as the rotation increases.",
  "直列": "Linear series",
  "直前の流路を保ちます": "Keep the channel just ahead.",
  "直動式の2ポート電磁弁": "Direct-acting two-port solenoid valve",
  "直接開路動作": "Direct open motion",
  "直流": "Direct current",
  "直流で赤と黒を逆に当てると、マイナスの値になる": "If you turn red and black in a direct current, it will be negative.",
  "直流電圧 V⎓": "DC voltage V⎓",
  "直流電圧 V⎓電池や直流電源のような直流を測ります。赤を+、黒を−に当てます。逆に当てるとマイナスの値になります。": "The DC voltage V⎓ is used to measure the DC current such as the battery and the DC power supply. Set red to + and black to -. Inversely, it will be negative.",
  "直流電流 A⎓": "DC current A",
  "直流電流 A⎓回路を切って、その切れ目にテスターを入れて(直列)測ります。この教材ではプラグを抜き、OFFのスイッチの両端にリードを当ててからプラグを差すと、ランプと直列になります。電源の両端に当てると短絡します。": "The DC current A⎓ circuit is cut off and a tester is placed in the cutoff and measured (in series). In this tutorial, the plug is unplugged, leads are placed on both ends of the OFF switch, and the plug is inserted, so that it is in line with the lamp. If you apply it to both ends of the power supply, it will short-circuit.",
  "直流電源": "DC power supply",
  "直流電源 +": "DC power supply +",
  "直流電源 −": "DC power supply -",
  "直流電源:交流をダイオードで一方向にそろえ(整流)、コンデンサでならして(平滑)、さらに回路で24Vちょうどに整えます(安定化)。しくみの欄の図を見てみよう。": "DC power supply: AC is directed in one direction by a diode (rectifying), smoothed by a capacitor (smoothing), and further adjusted to 24V by a circuit (stabilization). Let us look at the diagram of the structure column.",
  "直結": "Direct connection",
  "相": "Phase",
  "短絡!": "Short circuit!",
  "短絡! +24Vと0Vが直接つながったのでブレーカーが落ちました。原因の線を外してからブレーカーを入れ直してね。": "Short circuit! +24V and 0V were connected directly, so the breaker fell. Remove the cause line and then re-install the breaker.",
  "短絡! +24Vと0Vが直接つながるとブレーカーが落ちる": "Short circuit! +24V and 0V are directly connected, breaker is down.",
  "短絡! 何千Aもの電流が流れ、この教材ではMCCBの瞬時引き外しが作動しました。サーマルは熱で曲がるまで時間がかかるので、短絡には間に合いません。この教材では短絡の原因を取り除いた後、図のMCCBのレバーを押して復帰できます。": "Short circuit! Thermal takes time to be bent by heat, so it is not time for short circuits. In this teaching material, after removing the cause of short circuit, the MCCB can be reconnected by pushing the lever in the figure.",
  "短絡で遮断": "Short circuit cut off.",
  "短絡で非常に大きな電流が流れる": "A very large current flows through the short circuit.",
  "短絡はMCCBが一瞬で切る(サーマルでは間に合わない)": "MCCB cut short circuits in a moment.",
