  "細くて長い電線では電圧降下が大きくなる(5%超え)": "The voltage drop is greater (over 5%) in the thin and long wires.",
  "給水": "Water supply",
  "給水タンク": "Water tank",
  "給水タンクが登場。蛇口を「開」にすると水が減り、下限(FS1)まで減るとポンプが自動で動き出し、満水(FS2)で止まります。": "Open the outlet valve to lower the tank level. The pump starts automatically at the low-level float FS1 and stops at the full-level float FS2.",
  "給水中": "In the water supply",
  "絶対に飛ばしてはいけません": "You should never fly it .",
  "絶縁": "Insulation",
  "絶縁抵抗計(メガー)": "Insulation resistance meter (Meger)",
  "絶縁抵抗計(メガー)この例の100V電路（対地100V）では、0.1MΩ以上を判定の目安とします。実際の測定では停電と無電圧を確認し、電子機器の切り離し・試験電圧・判定値は対象機器の説明書に従います。": "Insulation resistance tester. This example uses 0.1 MΩ or more as its reference for a 100 V circuit (100 V to ground). In practice, isolate the circuit and verify absence of voltage. Follow the equipment manual for disconnecting electronics, selecting test voltage and assessing the reading.",
  "緑が消え、手を離しても赤だけが点いたままです。": "The green disappears, and when I take my hand off it, only the red remains lit.",
  "緑が消えて赤が点き、ファンは減速して止まります。手を離しても停止したままです。": "The green lights off and the red lights up, and the fan slows down and stops. I can take my hand off it, but it still stops.",
  "緑の運転灯（GL）が点き、赤が消えます。手を離しても緑は点いたままです。": "The green traffic light (GL) lights up and the red lights off. The green light remains lit even when you take your hand off it.",
  "線": "Line",
  "線が切れると0mA。正常な水位0%（4mA）と区別できる": "A broken loop gives 0 mA. A valid 0% level reading gives 4 mA.",
