  "軽い(120N)": "Lightweight (120N)",
  "近接(誘導形)": "Close contact (induced)",
  "近接(静電容量形)": "Close contact (electrostatic capacitive)",
  "近接センサー(誘導形)": "Proximity sensor (inductive type)",
  "近接センサー(誘導形)先端のコイルが作る磁界に金属が入ると、金属にうず電流が流れます。センサーはその影響でコイルの発振が変わるのを検出します。この教材の検出距離は鉄で8mm、アルミで3.5mmです。アルミを5mmと3mmで流して比べよう。": "Inductive proximity sensor. Eddy currents form in metal entering the sensing coil's field and change the coil's oscillation. Here the sensing range is 8 mm for iron and 3.5 mm for aluminum. Compare aluminum passing at 5 mm and 3 mm.",
  "近接センサー(静電容量形)": "Proximity sensor (electrostatic capacitive type)",
  "近接センサー(静電容量形)先端と物の間の静電容量(電気のたまりやすさ)の変化を見ます。金属以外の水・樹脂・紙にも反応します。タンクの外から中の水を検出する、などに使います。": "The electrostatic capacitance (ease of electricity) between the tip of the proximity sensor (electrostatic capacitance type) and the object is observed. It also reacts with water, resin and paper other than metal. It is used to detect the water inside the tank from outside, etc.",
  "近接センサーとの距離": "Distance to proximity sensor",
  "近接センサーと物の距離": "Proximity sensor distance to object",
  "逆転": "Inversion",
  "逆転 REV": "Inversion REV",
