  "通電時の": "I'm not sure what happened.",
  "通電：COMとa側が導通": "Power supply: COM and a side are connected.",
  "速さ": "Speed.",
  "速さは": "How fast?",
  "速さを調整します(メーターアウト)。しぼらないと端に勢いよくぶつかります。": "Adjust the speed (meter out). If you don't shake it, it will hit the edge with force.",
  "連続": "Continuum",
  "連続で何度も始動すると、大電流でモーターが熱くなります。": "When the motor is started several times in a row, it becomes hot with a large current.",
  "遊んで学ぶ": "Playing and learning",
  "遊んで学ぶ制御と電気": "Play-Learning Control and Electricity",
  "運転": "Driving",
  "運転スイッチ": "Drive switch",
  "運転スイッチが入っているため、LとNは": "Because there's a drive switch, L and N are not connected.",
  "運転スイッチが入っているため、LとNはモーターの巻線でつながっています。MΩの目盛りでは0.000と表示されます。外箱との絶縁は「L−金属外箱間」で確かめます。": "With the run switch closed, the motor winding connects L and N. The MΩ scale therefore reads 0.000. Measure between L and the metal enclosure to check insulation to the enclosure.",
  "運転スイッチが切れて巻線への経路が開いています": "The drive switch is off and the path to the wires is open.",
  "運転スイッチを入れたL−N間では、モーターの巻線を通るので小さな値を示す": "The values of the currents between L‐N are small because they pass through the winding of the motor.",
  "運転中": "Driving.",
  "過熱故障の目安": "Overheating failure criteria",
  "過負荷": "Overload",
  "過負荷が続く": "Overload continues.",
  "過負荷が続くと、サーマルが時間をおいて切れる": "If the overload continues, the thermostat will shut down in time.",
  "過負荷が続くと、電流の熱でバイメタルが曲がります。短絡で非常に大きな電流が流れると、電磁石が鉄片を直ちに引き寄せます。どちらも同じ引き外し機構を作動させ、ばねの力で接点を開きます。": "If the overload continues, the bimetal will bend due to the heat of the current. When a very large current flows through a short circuit, the electromagnet immediately attracts the iron pieces. Both operate the same pull-out mechanism and open the contact by spring force.",
  "過負荷で遮断": "Overloaded, cut off.",
  "過電圧(OV)": "Overvoltage (OV)",
  "過電圧(OV)で止まりました": "Overvoltage (OV) stopped.",
  "過電圧(OV)で止まりました。重い物を急に減速すると、モーターが発電機になって電気がインバータに戻り、中の電圧が上がりすぎます。減速時間をのばすか、実物では回生抵抗をつけます。": "The overvoltage (OV) stopped. When you slow down a heavy object suddenly, the motor becomes a generator, the electricity returns to the inverter, and the voltage inside rises too much. In the real object, the deceleration time is reduced or the regeneration resistance is added.",
  "過電流(OC)": "Overcurrent (OC)",
  "過電流(OC)で止まりました": "Overcurrent (OC) stopped.",
  "過電流(OC)で止まりました。加速時間が短すぎて、モーターに大きな電流を流さないと間に合わなかったためです。インバータは自分とモーターを守るために出力を止めます。加速時間をのばして「アラーム解除」。": "It stopped due to over current (OC). The acceleration time was too short to be able to do so without applying a large current to the motor. The inverter stops output to protect itself and the motor. The acceleration time is reduced by \"unlocking the alarm\".",
